### How it works

`maxResponseSize` is enforced by intercepting the response stream and reading it in chunks. Ky creates a new `ReadableStream` that reads from the original response body but only up to the specified `maxResponseSize`. When the total size of the read data exceeds `maxResponseSize`, Ky stops reading and closes the stream, effectively truncating the response.

